•	Vendor User Stories

1.	US-V01: Vendor Registration and Login
-	User Story: As a vendor, I want to register for an account and securely log in, so that I can access and manage my surplus food listings and orders.
-	Acceptance Criteria:
	The system allows vendors to register by providing the required business details and contact information.
	The system validates the registration details and prevents registration if required fields are missing or invalid.
	The system allows registered vendors to log in using their credentials.
	The system displays an error message when registration or login fails.
	Vendor account credentials are stored securely.

2.	US-V02: Creating Surplus Food Listings
-	User Story: As a vendor, I want to create food listings with the item’s name, description, category, quantity, price, expiration and collection deadline, so that customers can view and reserve available surplus food.
-	Acceptance Criteria:
	The system allows vendors to create a listing by entering the food item’s name, description, category, quantity, initial price, minimum, expiration date and time, and collection deadline.
	The system requires all mandatory fields to be completed before a listing is created.
	The system validates that the quantity and initial selling price is greater than 0.
	The system ensures that the collection deadline does not exceed the food’s expiration time.
	The system displays successfully created listings to customers while the food is available for reservation.

3.	US-V03: Editing Listings and Managing Quantities
-	User Story: As a vendor, I want to edit my food listings and update their available quantities, and have listings automatically marked as unavailable passed their collection deadline, so that customers see accurate information and are not able to reserve food that is no longer available.
-	Acceptance Criteria:
	The system allows vendors to edit the details of their existing food listings.
	The system allows vendors to update the available quantity of a listing.
	The system prevents the available quantity to be set to negative value.
	The system automatically marks listings as unavailable once their collection deadline has passed.
	The system prevents customers from reserving listings that are unavailable or have 0 remaining quantity.

4.	US-V04: Setting Initial and Minimum Selling Prices
-	User Story: As a vendor, I want to set an initial price and a minimum price for each listing, so that I can control the starting price and set a lowest price the system can apply
-	Acceptance Criteria:
	The system allows vendors to set an initial selling price for each food listing.
	The system allows vendors to set a minimum selling price for each food listing.
	The system ensures that both prices are greater than 0
	The system ensures that the minimum selling price does not exceed the initial selling price.
	The system stores the vendor’s prices and makes them available to the dynamic pricing system.

5.	US-V05: Automatic Price Reductions as Expiration Approaches
-	User Story: As a vendor, I want to have the prices automatically reduced as the collection deadline approaches (without going below my set minimum price), so that customers are encouraged to purchase the surplus food before it expires.
-	Acceptance Criteria:
	The system automatically reduces the selling prices according to a predefined discount schedule as the collection deadline approaches.
	The system calculates the discounted price based on the listing’s initial selling price.
	The system ensures that the selling price never falls below the vendors specified minimum selling price.
	The system updates the displayed selling price whenever a new discount is applied.
	The system stops applying price reductions when the minimum price is reached or the listing becomes unavailable.
	The system adjusts price reductions based on customer demand, with slower reductions when demand is high and faster reductions when demand is low.

6.	US-V06: Managing Reservations and Pickups
-	User Story: As a vendor, I want to view and manage customer reservations, track their status, and confirm pickups, so that I can prepare orders and keep track of collected food.
-	Acceptance Criteria:
	The system allows vendors to view customer reservations, including the reserved items, quantities and collection times.
	The system allows vendors to track reservation status, including confirmed, collected, and cancelled.
	The system updates the available quantity when a reservation is created or cancelled, including when the 10-minute reservation hold expires.
	The system allows the vendor to confirm when a customer collects their reserved food.
	The system prevents vendors from confirming a pickup for a cancelled reservation.

